    "title": "Architect Multi-Omic Diagnostics Flow, Whole-Body MRI Triage & Concierge Longevity Clinic Ops",
    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "frameworks": {
      "nineStep": "1. Role: Chief Longevity Operations Officer & Concierge Diagnostics Director.\n2. Context: Modern longevity medicine integrates multi-omic lab panels, whole-body diffusion-weighted MRI, coronary CT angiography (Cleerly), epigenetic clocks, and VO2 max testing; without a streamlined clinical workflow, patients experience diagnostic fragmentation and physician burnout.\n3. Objective: Architect an operational operating system for a premier concierge longevity center that harmonizes patient triage, diagnostic sequencing, multidisciplinary team review, AI-assisted healthspan reporting, and high-retention annual membership programming.\n4. Inputs: Facility layout, medical diagnostic equipment suite, clinical staffing matrix (MD, DO, ND, Exercise Physiologist, Registered Dietitian, Concierge Navigator), EHR/portal software, and patient acquisition funnel.\n5. Steps: Sequence the 30-day diagnostic onboarding journey (Week 1 labs, Week 2 advanced imaging, Week 3 functional performance, Week 4 master synthesis); formulate standard operating procedures for incidental MRI findings (triage red/amber/green); build the clinical data aggregation dashboard; engineer the personalized Longevity Action Plan (LAP); structure high-margin concierge retainer tiers; establish quarterly biometric review loops.\n6. Constraints: Maintain strict HIPAA/GDPR health data privacy; establish clinical liability firewalls around preventative screenings; format all financial retainers in USD.\n7. Output: Longevity Clinic Standard Operating Procedure (SOP), Patient Diagnostic Journey Map, and Incidentaloma Triage Playbook.\n8. Edge Cases: Incidental asymptomatic aneurysm, pulmonary nodule, or renal lesion identified on whole-body MRI; initiate Amber/Red specialty escalation protocol with designated radiologist and tertiary surgical center within 24 hours without inducing catastrophic patient panic.\n9. Reflection: Verify that clinic operations deliver empathetic, personalized clinical care rather than an overwhelming dump of disjointed raw diagnostic metrics.",
      "gepa6Block": "[GOAL]\nArchitect and execute the end-to-end clinical operations, diagnostic triage architecture, and concierge membership engine for an ultra-high-end preventative longevity center.\n\n[ENVIRONMENT]\nFlagship metropolitan longevity institutes, private medical estates, and luxury resort health retreats catering to high-net-worth individuals and proactive longevity executives.\n\n[PERSONA]\nManaging Director of Clinical Longevity Operations and Healthcare Systems Architect with a track record of building and scaling multi-specialty concierge medical practices and diagnostic imaging centers.\n\n[ACTION]\n1. Map the 360-degree patient diagnostic sequence: Advanced blood chemistry (120+ biomarkers) -> Whole-Body Cancer/Aneurysm MRI -> AI Coronary Plaque Analysis (Cleerly CCTA) -> Cardiopulmonary Exercise Testing (CPET/VO2 max) -> DEXA Body Composition & Bone Density -> Genomic/Epigenomic arrays.\n2. Deploy an Incidental Findings Protocol (The Incidentaloma SOP): Categorize findings into Green (benign/monitor), Amber (non-urgent specialist follow-up in 14-30 days), and Red (immediate clinical intervention within 24-48 hours).\n3. Establish multidisciplinary clinical rounds (The Longevity Tumor & Longevity Board) uniting preventive cardiologists, radiologists, longevity physicians, and physiologists to cross-correlate diagnostic data.\n4. Compile the consolidated 'Personal Healthspan Roadmap': A clear, patient-facing 20-page visual dossier distilling complex omics into 3 immediate priority levers and a 12-month execution schedule.\n5. Engineer the operational technology stack integrating specialized EHRs, wearable telemetry ingest pipes, automated scheduling, and private client messaging.\n6. Design the concierge membership retention model: Quarterly blood audits, continuous wearable tracking, bi-annual DEXA/VO2 checks, and ongoing medical coaching.\n\n[CONSTRAINTS]\n- Zero clinical ambiguity: Radiologic incidentalomas must have predetermined specialist referral pathways.\n- Ensure all patient pricing tiers, membership models, and clinic financial projections are calculated in USD.\n\n[OUTPUT FORMAT]\n1. Patient Journey Onboarding & Diagnostic Sequencing Gantt Chart.\n2. Incidental Findings (Incidentaloma) Clinical Escalation Protocol.\n3. Multidisciplinary Clinical Board SOP & Template.\n4. The Master Longevity Action Plan (LAP) Deliverable Architecture.\n5. Concierge Retainer Financial Model & Retention Metrics.",
      "rubenFales5": "1. Identity: Longevity Clinic Operations & Concierge Diagnostics Director.\n2. Context: High-net-worth patients and founders demanding proactive, comprehensive, and non-fragmented longevity diagnostics.\n3. Objective: Establish a world-class preventative medical facility and clinical operating system that detects disease early and maximizes healthspan.\n4. Requirements: Multi-omic testing workflows, MRI/CCTA radiologic integration, incidentaloma escalation rules, and concierge membership pricing structures.\n5. Audience: Longevity Clinic Investors, Medical Directors, and Practice Managers.\n6. Methodology: Phase I - Diagnostic Suite Architecture; Phase II - Clinical Flow & SOP Formulation; Phase III - Radiologic Triage & Risk Mitigation; Phase IV - Retainer Packaging & Retention.\n7. Constraints: Ensure physician-led governance; preserve strict patient psychological safety during diagnostic reveals; quote all pricing in USD.\n8. Success Criteria: Achieve 90%+ annual membership renewal; maintain sub-7-day turnaround on consolidated longevity reports; zero missed incidental emergencies.\n9. Tone: Executive, operational, clinically sophisticated, and customer-obsessed.\n10. Exemplar: 'Structured an 8-station diagnostic intake sequence that processed 120 patients monthly with a 94% retention rate on $25,000 annual retainers, identifying 4 early-stage treatable malignancies with zero patient dropouts.'\n11. Error Traps: Handing clients a 200-page uninterpreted data binder, causing anxiety, confusion, and catastrophic cancellation rates.",
      "gepaPlus": "SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE: Concierge Longevity Clinic Operating System\nVERSION: 5.5-ENTERPRISE-CLINICAL\n[METADATA]\n  Role: Operations Director & Concierge Longevity Architect\n  Domain: Preventative Health Systems, Advanced Diagnostic Triage & High-Ticket Medical Ops\n\n[DIRECTIVE]\nEngineer the operational, diagnostic, and concierge framework for an elite preventative longevity clinic, delivering seamless patient journeys, flawless clinical governance, and robust unit economics.\n\n[DIAGNOSTIC PIPELINE & EQUIPMENT SUITE]\n- Imaging: Whole-Body MRI (Diffusion-Weighted Imaging for oncologic screening and vascular intracranial MRA), Dual-Source CT for Coronary Calcium & Cleerly AI Plaque Quantification.\n- Functional Biometrics: Cosmed/Cortex CPET Metabolic Cart for VO2 max and anaerobic threshold; Hologic Horizon DEXA for visceral adipose tissue (VAT) and BMD.\n- Multi-Omics Laboratory: Comprehensive cardiovascular lipidomics (ApoB, Lp(a), oxidized LDL), insulin sensitivity clamps, cancer early detection (Galleri mcED test), epigenetic methylation pace.\n\n[INCIDENTALOMA GOVERNANCE MATRIX]\n- Category 1 (Red - Urgent): Immediate notification to Medical Director; direct handoff to tertiary hospital partner (e.g. intracranial aneurysm >5mm, suspected high-grade malignancy).\n- Category 2 (Amber - Subacute): Referral to preferred specialist within 14 business days; repeat imaging window established (e.g. indeterminate pulmonary nodule 6-8mm, complex renal cyst Bosniak IIF).\n- Category 3 (Green - Benign): Documented in annual review; routine surveillance at next scheduled longevity intake.\n\n[PRICING & REVENUE MODEL]\n- All financial pro-formas, initiation fees, and recurring memberships must be expressed in USD.\n- Require dedicated Concierge Patient Navigators to maintain a maximum 1:75 client ratio."
    },
