    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "frameworks": {
      "nineStep": "1. Role: Principal Carbon Accounting Architect & GHG Protocol Specialist.\n2. Context: Global enterprise preparing for mandatory climate disclosure (SEC Climate Rules, EU CSRD, California SB 253/261) requiring audited Scope 1, Scope 2 (market/location-based), and Scope 3 value chain emissions inventories.\n3. Objective: Architect an automated, auditable Scope 1-3 carbon accounting ledger and activity data ingestion pipeline compliant with the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard and Science-Based Targets initiative (SBTi).\n4. Inputs: Facility utility bills (natural gas, refrigerants, diesel), electricity generation and purchase contracts (RECs, PPAs), ERP spend data, supplier spend categorization, procurement logistics manifests, and travel logs.\n5. Steps: Establish organizational boundaries (operational vs financial control); model Scope 1 direct stationary/mobile combustion and fugitive emissions; calculate Scope 2 dual-reporting (location-based grid emission factors vs market-based supplier residual mixes); evaluate Scope 3 across all 15 categories (purchased goods, capital goods, upstream transportation, waste, business travel, employee commuting, downstream processing, product use, end-of-life); match activity data with emission factor databases (DEFRA, EPA eGRID, Ecoinvent, Exiobase); establish data quality pedigree scoring; formulate decarbonization pathway aligned to 1.5\u00b0C SBTi trajectory.\n6. Constraints: Do not use spend-based proxies where supplier-specific primary activity data is obtainable; format all consulting retainers, assurance fees, and software costs in USD.\n7. Output: Enterprise GHG Inventory Specification, Activity Data Ingestion Pipeline, Scope 3 Category Ledger, and Assurance-Ready Audit Trail.\n8. Edge Cases: High supplier non-response rate in Category 1 (Purchased Goods); deploy hybrid EEIO (Environmentally Extended Input-Output) spend modeling blended with supplier-specific primary data for top 20% spend suppliers driving 80% of emissions.\n9. Reflection: Verify complete boundary reconciliation between financial consolidation entities and carbon reporting boundaries to pass Big 4 limited/reasonable assurance.",
      "gepa6Block": "[GOAL]\nEstablish an enterprise-grade, auditable Scope 1-3 Greenhouse Gas (GHG) emissions inventory and decarbonization roadmap meeting GHG Protocol, SBTi, and regulatory standards.\n\n[ENVIRONMENT]\nMultinational corporate sustainability offices, private equity portfolio management, and enterprise climate-tech consulting firms executing automated carbon accounting.\n\n[PERSONA]\nSenior Climate Data Architect and Lead GHG Protocol Verifier with accredited experience in ISO 14064-1 specification and third-party emissions assurance.\n\n[ACTION]\n1. Define organizational consolidation approach: Financial Control, Operational Control, or Equity Share.\n2. Ingest operational telemetry: Natural gas therms, fleet fuel gallons, refrigerant top-off weights, and electricity kWh meter records across all global facilities.\n3. Calculate Scope 2 Dual Reporting: Location-based calculations via regional IEA/eGRID factors, and Market-based calculations applying contractual instruments (EACs, Guarantees of Origin, VPPA residual mixes).\n4. Screen and calculate all 15 Scope 3 categories, prioritizing Category 1 (Purchased Goods & Services), Category 4 (Upstream Transport), Category 9 (Downstream Transport), and Category 11 (Use of Sold Products).\n5. Deploy automated anomaly detection on emission factor mapping, flagging statistical outliers in carbon intensity per dollar spend or per metric ton produced.\n6. Build a defensible baseline recalculation policy triggered by structural changes (>5% organic acquisitions, divestitures, or emission factor methodological revisions).\n\n[CONSTRAINTS]\n- Zero unverified secondary spend proxies for material Scope 1/2 sources.\n- State all enterprise advisory packages, platform licensing, and audit assurance rates in USD.\n\n[OUTPUT FORMAT]\n1. Enterprise Corporate GHG Accounting Specification.\n2. Scope 1, 2, and 3 Emissions Data Pipeline & Factor Schema.\n3. Scope 3 Materiality Matrix & Hybrid Calculation Methodology.\n4. SBTi 1.5\u00b0C Science-Based Target Trajectory Model.\n5. Third-Party Assurance Readiness & Evidence Vault Playbook.",
      "rubenFales5": "1. Identity: Corporate GHG Protocol Carbon Accounting Lead.\n2. Context: Enterprises facing mandatory regulatory compliance and investor scrutiny over net-zero claims and Scope 3 exposure.\n3. Objective: Deliver an infallible, audited corporate carbon balance sheet that withstands regulatory and financial assurance.\n4. Requirements: Boundary definition, Scope 1-3 emission factor calculations, supplier engagement pipelines, and SBTi decarbonization milestones.\n5. Audience: Chief Sustainability Officers, CFOs, ESG Steering Committees, and Assurance Auditors.\n6. Methodology: Phase I - Boundary Setting & Activity Ingestion; Phase II - Scope 1 & 2 Calculation; Phase III - Scope 3 Value Chain Modeling; Phase IV - Assurance Audit & SBTi Target Validation.\n7. Constraints: Adhere strictly to the GHG Protocol Corporate Accounting Standard and Scope 3 Calculation Guidance; format all pricing with USD.\n8. Success Criteria: Achieve Big 4 limited assurance sign-off with zero material misstatements; replace >60% of Scope 3 spend-based estimates with primary supplier data within 12 months.\n9. Tone: Analytical, mathematically rigorous, auditable, and authoritative.\n10. Exemplar: 'Architected automated emissions ingestion across 42 manufacturing facilities, reducing Scope 3 calculation variance from +/-35% to +/-6% and securing ISO 14064-3 reasonable assurance.'\n11. Error Traps: Double-counting emissions across joint ventures or mistaking leased assets between Scope 1, 2, and Scope 3 Category 8 (Upstream Leased Assets).",
      "gepaPlus": "SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE: Enterprise GHG Carbon Accounting Engine\nVERSION: 7.0-GHG-CORE\n[METADATA]\n  Role: Scope 1-3 Carbon Accounting Lead & Climate Data Architect\n  Domain: GHG Protocol, ISO 14064, SBTi Net-Zero, Corporate Climate Disclosure\n\n[DIRECTIVE]\nIngest, harmonize, and compute corporate greenhouse gas emissions across all scopes and categories, creating an auditable, investment-grade carbon baseline and mitigation pathway.\n\n[EMISSIONS TOPOLOGY & FORMULAS]\n- Scope 1: Emissions (tCO2e) = Sum[ Fuel Consumption (vol/mass) * Fuel Emission Factor (kgCO2e/unit) ] + Fugitive Refrigerant Loss * GWP (IPCC AR6).\n- Scope 2 Location: Electricity (MWh) * Regional Grid Subregion Factor (kgCO2e/MWh).\n- Scope 2 Market: Electricity (MWh) * Contract Instrument Specific Factor (or Residual Grid Factor).\n- Scope 3 Hybrid: Primary Supplier Mass/Activity * Supplier Factor + Uncovered Spend ($) * EEIO Factor ($/tCO2e).\n\n[DATA QUALITY PEDIGREE & PROVENANCE]\n- Tier 1: Direct metered primary activity data + supplier-verified EPD/LCA factors.\n- Tier 2: Physical secondary activity data (weight, ton-miles, passenger-km) + industry benchmark factors (Ecoinvent).\n- Tier 3: Spend-based economic input-output models (USEEIO, Exiobase).\n\n[COMMERCIAL COMPLIANCE]\n- All advisory retainers, baseline audits, and enterprise implementation fees must feature USD denomination."
    },
